("A machine learning model fits its training data almost perfectly but predicts poorly on new data. This problem is called:",
 "Overfitting", ["Underfitting", "Multicollinearity", "Survivorship bias"],
 "An overfit model learns noise in the training data and generalizes badly. Underfitting is the opposite: a model too simple to capture the pattern even in training data."),
("Grouping companies into clusters by similar financial traits, with no target variable given, is an example of:",
 "Unsupervised learning", ["Supervised learning", "Reinforcement learning", "Linear regression"],
 "Clustering finds structure in unlabeled data, so it is unsupervised. Supervised learning needs a labeled target, as in regression or classification."),
